x.q('instruction_startup_and_response_admission',0,44,54,'instruction_assembly prompt_dispatch_carriers','Dispatch-affecting assembly/plans/renderers/binding policies use canonical startup/registry admission, never scans/shell/loaders/local registry/duplicate selection. Selection derives admitted startup replay; query-only lookup gives no authority and advice needs admission/validation. Responses need admission against selected target/asset response contract before assurance/continuation/residual/closure; transport,self-report,prompt/parse shape never closure. Every F_P boundary with absent/unresolved/unadmitted/nonmatching startup blocks before worker/plugin/evaluator invocation or response/assurance/continuation/residual/closure consumption.')
x.q('review_and_dependency_sufficiency',0,50,52,'instruction_assembly','F_P plan review is attributed judgment evidence, not dispatch approval,binding,selection,rendering or response admission; later F_D checks structural/identity/dependency/admission predicates while judgment retains basis/uncertainty. Reject build/test/proof/release/deploy/target-artifact F_P dispatch if required dependency sufficiency unknown. F_D establishes declared prerequisite closure from admitted graph,lineage,proof policy,typed gaps; separately require owner semantic sufficiency. Explicit dependency-disambiguation traversal may precede sufficiency only to propose dependency nodes/edges/gaps, never claim artifact/proof/release/closure.',exceptions=['Explicitly scoped dependency-disambiguation may dispatch with unknown sufficiency to produce candidate dependencies or typed gaps only.'])
