x.q('validation_total_inventory_and_derivation',3,106,127,'whole_program_validation','Fail closed for empty/partial/caller-selected inventory missing required programs,functions,graphs,vectors,interfaces,starts,contracts,implementations,source identities. Derive graph outputs through declared input/vector contracts; reject undeclared loci,unsatisfied dependencies,unreachable vectors,non-derivable outputs,ambiguous duplicate ids. Every materialized vector gets exactly one target-carrier and one closure relation or typed unresolved-semantic result. Prompt assets retain renderer,constructor,digest policy,output,authority,proof,node,fold relations; text/files alone are not contract truth.')
x.q('validation_no_hidden_authority',3,129,151,'whole_program_validation direct_hog_execution','Plugins/bindings use runtime typed constructors/admission; reject unknown/prohibited authority fields, do not strip. Validation projects/rejects starts,entries,vectors,membership,seams,output admission,consequences,catalog options without executing. Reject bare vectors as public authority,overlay shortcuts,schedule topology,plugin-file result law,unavailable consequences,adapter-route bind law,ambiguous entry. GTL owns One Surface order and published recursion; HoG traverses; ABG conserves four semantic owners and distinct intent/invocation/evidence/action-result/continuation boundaries. No helper/worker/SDK/CLI/fixture second controller.')
